course: dictionary
lesson: 6877
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them shows which one you need. Overlook can mean to miss something, to forgive a mistake, or to see over a place from above.
explain: In maths, «Don't overlook the units» means don't miss them. If a teacher says, «I will overlook the small spelling mistake», she means she will forgive it and not punish it. The words after overlook are your clue.
explain: When you meet overlook, try each meaning in the sentence. Does «miss» fit? Does «forgive» fit? Does «see over» fit? The one that makes sense is the right one.
fact: Overlook is a verb: overlook, overlooks, overlooked, overlooking.
fact: «Overlook» can mean to fail to notice something, to forgive a mistake, or to look down on a place from above.
fact: In «people the world often overlooks», overlooked means not noticed or not given enough credit.
fact: In «her part was overlooked at first», people did not notice her part at the start.
fact: (US) An overlook is a high place where you stop to look at a view.
exercise: «Don't overlook the units when you write your answer.» What does overlook mean here? | *Miss or fail to notice | Look down on from a high window | Read out loud carefully | Forgive and ignore
exercise: «The teacher chose to overlook the small spelling mistake.» What does overlook mean? | Shout about it to the class | *Forgive it and not punish it | Look at it closely with a magnifier | Write it out again neatly
exercise: «The hotel window overlooks the lake.» What does overlooks mean? | Hides the lake from view | *Lets you see the lake from above | Floats on top of the lake | Swims across the lake
test: «Many kind people are overlooked by the newspapers.» What does overlooked mean? | Forgiven for a mistake | *Not noticed or not given credit | Sent a letter | Painted in bright colours
test: Ella says the hill's overlook has the best view in town. What is an overlook in this sentence? | *A high place where you stop to look at a view | A tunnel under the hill | A rule for climbing | A shop that sells maps
exam: Jayden reads, «She decided to overlook his rudeness.» What does overlook mean? | Make a copy of | Notice and write down | *Forgive and decide not to punish | Look at from a window above
